  reading: Larger x raises f_theta = mu + x mu' toward 1, which LOWERS the khronon's net self-force kernel at every k (to the Jeans form 1 - k^2/(a mu)^2 as x -> infinity). In v3's PN system a large early x therefore stiffens the khronon; it does not release it. 'Hold off before z_x' is not self-consistent; the linear (x = 0) growth results are, if anything, optimistic.
